      "evidence": "Definition of backup duties in Ashford's framework: duties that apply when primary duties are not feasible, but remain binding.",
      "weight": 0.2,
      "depends_on": [1]
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "claim": "Recognizing backup duties lets us acknowledge criticisms that effective altruism may be only a \"band‑aid\" solution.",
      "evidence": "Ashford argues that even if effective altruism does not fully solve global poverty, the existence of backup duties means we still have a moral role to play.",
      "weight": 0.25,
      "depends_on": [2]
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "claim": "By acknowledging the criticism while also pointing to backup duties, we can diffuse the force of that criticism.",
      "evidence": "Ashford uses the backup‑duty move to show that the criticism does not nullify our moral responsibility; it merely reshapes it.",
      "weight": 0.15,
      "depends_on": [3]
    },
    {
